(5678255, 824623, 18563, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SaraR:</b></div><hr/><i> I was certain this was going to take the blue ribbon - what is with the 13 votes of 3 or under! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was trying to figure that out myself! I know this image might not appeal to everyone''s taste but I have never scored an image that low unless it DNMC <b>and</b> lacked in the quality department. :S<br/> <br/>I would love to hear from a few of the 13</td>', 'Originally posted by SaraR: I was certain this was going to take the blue ribbon - what is with the 13 votes of 3 or under!   I was trying to figure that out myself! I know this image might not appeal to everyone''s taste but I have never scored an image that low unless it DNMC and lacked in the quality department. :S I would love to hear from a few of the 13', '2009-10-07 11:26:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5678259, 824528, 32767, '<td valign="top">This is great. Would loved to has seen this on the front page. Cheers!</td>', 'This is great. Would loved to has seen this on the front page. Cheers!', '2009-10-07 11:34:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5678322, 824402, 90600, '<td valign="top">Thanks, Jaded. I think it''s clear by the voting this is not the kind of image that will do well here. It''s my only photo that anyone made a "fave" and yet it is also my lowest scoring photo! LOL. I wanted to try and submit something edgier since my tame shots were really not doing very well. Oh well. I can''t seem to figure DPC out. Will have to keep working harder for some magic shots!</td>', 'Thanks, Jaded. I think it''s clear by the voting this is not the kind of image that will do well here. It''s my only photo that anyone made a "fave" and yet it is also my lowest scoring photo! LOL. I wanted to try and submit something edgier since my tame shots were really not doing very well. Oh well. I can''t seem to figure DPC out. Will have to keep working harder for some magic shots!', '2009-10-07 12:31:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5678340, 824713, 99981, '<td valign="top">At least for me this is a hard shot to comment. I can see something poor on the woman''s face, but wouldn''t know what it is. Since you said, i agree it''s the light. I probabbly didn''t know what was it because i don''t know anything about this subject (light and stuff). I read a few days ago some things about reflectors, just a white board or paper to reflect the natural light on her face, i''m sure you know that kind of thing because you have 94 years and 3 in dpc (:D) but maybe that would help. The worst part seems to be the left one, the light there doesn''t help her skin, hair and makeup. <br/>Talking about the composition, i think the little piece of background at the right is distracting. I would prefer to see background everywhere than just that little piece. But the best choice would be a different perspective showing only her face and the hat in my opinion. This perspective is giving more emphasis to the face than the hat. <br/>The makeup is nice and i like her boring expression. And i think it meets the challenge well. <br/>I hope i could be helpfull and you don''t get offender by my giant newbie comment. <br/>Cheers!<br/> <br/>Pedro<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-10-07 11:41:44.</i></td>', 'At least for me this is a hard shot to comment. I can see something poor on the woman''s face, but wouldn''t know what it is. Since you said, i agree it''s the light. I probabbly didn''t know what was it because i don''t know anything about this subject (light and stuff). I read a few days ago some things about reflectors, just a white board or paper to reflect the natural light on her face, i''m sure you know that kind of thing because you have 94 years and 3 in dpc (:D) but maybe that would help. The worst part seems to be the left one, the light there doesn''t help her skin, hair and makeup. Talking about the composition, i think the little piece of background at the right is distracting. I would prefer to see background everywhere than just that little piece. But the best choice would be a different perspective showing only her face and the hat in my opinion. This perspective is giving more emphasis to the face than the hat. The makeup is nice and i like her boring expression. And i think it meets the challenge well. I hope i could be helpfull and you don''t get offender by my giant newbie comment. Cheers! Pedro', '2009-10-07 12:40:21.000000', '2009-10-07 12:41:44.000000', 0),
